  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 5♣. As West has shown an 8 card heart suit with his opening 4 heart bid, South must win the opening lead to have any chance. 11 tricks seem very far away. It seems South will have to endplay West at least once and possibly squeeze East.\n\nSouth should start by cashing dummy's top clubs. When East discards, South should draw West's last trump. South's only remaining technical chance is that West started with 1813 distribution.\n\nSouth should cash a top spade and the ♦A and exit in hearts. West must win this trick. Down to all hearts, he must concede a ruff and discard. The ruff and discard does not gain a trick as South could have scored his trumps separately anyway.\n\nSouth should, in fact, leave West on lead by discarding diamonds from both hands. West plays another heart. This time dummy's last diamond is discarded. East is trump squeezed on this trick.\n\nIf East comes down to 1 diamond, South ruffs and can set up a diamond by ruffing in dummy. If East discards a spade, a long spade in North's hand can be established by ruffing in the closed hand.",
